  "instructions": [
    "Pickled onions (make ahead if you can): put the sliced onion in a heatproof jar or bowl. Bring the vinegar, water, salt, and sugar to a boil; boil 2 minutes; pour over the onions and let cool.",
    "Beans: heat a little oil in a pan over medium heat. Add the cumin seeds, crushed red pepper, and jalapeno if using; heat until fragrant, about a minute. Add the beans and cook, mashing as they heat, until thick but not pasty, about 8-10 minutes. Take off the heat and stir in a squeeze of lemon juice.",
    "Beef version: heat a pan over medium-high heat. Add the ground beef as one big clump and sear/brown the outside before breaking it up; then cook through, breaking it into crumbles. Turn OFF the heat and stir in the taco seasoning.",
    "Chicken version (instead of step 3): season the chicken pieces with salt and pepper; cook in a hot oiled pan until cooked through and lightly browned, about 8-10 minutes. (A marinade is fine sometimes, but plain salt and pepper is the norm.)",
    "Salad: toss the sliced romaine and diced tomatoes with salt and pepper.",
    "Sauce: stir all the sauce ingredients together.",
    "Warm each tortilla in a dry pan until soft and pliable.",
    "Build each burrito: sauce down the middle, then beans, protein, lettuce-tomato salad, and pickled onions. Fold in the sides and roll up tight."
  ],
